\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Bride-groom, Thou art mine;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Jesus, Lamb divine!
\par Saved from sin, to Thee I render
\par thanks for love so pure and tender
\par which has made me Thine,
\par Jesus, Lamb divine!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy pervading love
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Brings strength from above
\par \cf1 When Thy friendly eyes behold me\cf0 
\par and Thou drawest me towards Thee,
\par  Thy pervading love
\par  brings strength from above.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   May my faith's bright light
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  never turn to night.
\par  With Thy Spirit's oil supply me,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 lest my soul should e'er deny Thee.
\par and thus turn to night
\par my faith's shining light.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Faithful unto Thee
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  I shall ever be.
\par Thy great love I must be praising
\par thereby high Thine honour raising;
\par I shall ever be
\par Faithful unto Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Here thro' scorn and frown,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 There the glorious crown!
\par Here in hoping and believing,
\par there in seeing and receiving:
\par after scorn and frown
\par \pard      comes the glorious crown!  
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

